note Word access for the aligned paths. b8 is the caller's 8-byte-aligned copy of the input lent a
note second time as ulong cells (b views the same bytes), so one load brings 8 bytes. Swapping the
note bytes inside each 32-bit half (two mask-and-shift steps; the constants stay in registers) turns
note little-endian bytes b0..b7 into the big-endian words b0..b3 (low half) and b4..b7 (high half).
note Each word is stored duplicated, as expand requires.
fn blk8 b8 view ulong 512 q ulong w edit ulong 64 to void
for i ulong 8
x = get b8 add q i
y = or shl and x 71777214294589695 8 and shr x 8 71777214294589695
y = or shl and y 281470681808895 16 and shr y 16 281470681808895
j = mul i 2
t = shl y 32
put w j or t shr t 32
put w add j 1 or and y 18446744069414584320 shr y 32
end
end

note the padded tail b[off..n) (less than 64 bytes), read as words through b8 (the bytes past n
note are inside the caller's 4096-byte copy and are masked off here): the word holding byte n keeps
note its k valid bytes and gets 0x80 after them, later words are zero, the 64-bit bit count goes in
note words 14 and 15; a second block when the tail is 56 bytes or more
fn tail8 h edit uint 8 b8 view ulong 512 off ulong n ulong w edit ulong 64 to void
blk8 b8 shr off 3 w
r = sub n off
fw = shr r 2
k = and r 3
sh = mul k 8
v = get w fw
v = and v shl 4294967295 sub 32 sh
v = and v 4294967295
v = or v shl 128 sub 24 sh
put w fw or v shl v 32
i = add fw 1
while lt i 16 bound 16
put w i 0
i = add i 1
end
if ge r 56
expand w
rounds h w
for j ulong 14
put w j 0
end
end
bits = mul n 8
v = shr bits 32
put w 14 or v shl v 32
v = and bits 4294967295
put w 15 or v shl v 32
expand w
rounds h w
end

note the digest of h as 32 bytes packed little endian into w[0..4): word i holds the big-endian
note bytes of h[2i] then h[2i+1], so the caller copies the digest out of w with memcpy
fn digest8 h edit uint 8 w edit ulong 64 to void
for i ulong 4
j = mul i 2
x = or ulong get h j shl ulong get h add j 1 32
y = or shl and x 71777214294589695 8 and shr x 8 71777214294589695
y = or shl and y 281470681808895 16 and shr y 16 281470681808895
put w i y
end
end

note SHA-256 of the n < 4096 bytes in b8, state in locals only (sha256_hash's short path)
fn oneshot b8 view ulong 512 n ulong w edit ulong 64 to void
if ge n 4096
trap 3
end
h = new uint 8 0
initiv h
off = ulong 0
while le add off 64 n bound 64
blk8 b8 shr off 3 w
expand w
rounds h w
off = add off 64
end
tail8 h b8 off n w
digest8 h w
end

fn omsha c edit uchar 104 b view uchar 4096 n ulong op ulong w edit ulong 64 b8 view ulong 512 to void
if eq op 0
init c
ret
end
if eq op 1
absorb c b n w
ret
end
if eq op 2
final c w
ret
end
if eq op 3
oneshot b8 n w
ret
end
trap 9
end

#### c2-05723 sha256=8eb77cc5574ac4bbd6f369f42c64454566daa0f01df77e8e9011329ee23b9b06 len=358
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note Alias-violation control for the CURRENT language (OMEGESE 9.4): the arrays of one call must be
note distinct names, so passing one array as both an edit and a view argument is refused (error 19).
fn mix a edit uchar 4 b view uchar 4 to void
put a 0 get b 0
end
fn main to int
x = new uchar 4 0
mix x x
ret 0
end

#### c2-05724 sha256=2fe76d4c44b3e3faf6bfd250ebec794ba5b3d11b6b9199366549b664d219cc38 len=887
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note Weakened-guard witness (#748): write 4 bytes from offset o = 2^64-2 of a 4-byte array to /dev/null.
note o and k = 4 are the issue's overflow pair (fixtures/obligations.txt, first slice row): the
note wrapped sum o+k = 2 <= len 4 is TRUE but k <= len - o is FALSE. A correct compiler traps 3
note before the system call (exit 103, no output). A compiler whose check is the wrapped sum lets
note the call run; /dev/null accepts the bytes without reading them, so the mutant path is
note deterministic: it prints WRAPPED_SLICE_ACCEPTED_4 and a newline and exits 0.
text devnull "/dev/null"
text accepted "WRAPPED_SLICE_ACCEPTED_4\n"
fn main to int
a = new uchar 4 0
f = fopen devnull 0 len devnull 1 0
if lt f 0
ret 90
end
o = ulong 18446744073709551614
r = write int f a o 4
if eq r 4
w = write 1 accepted 0 len accepted
ret 0
end
ret 91
end

#### c2-05725 sha256=eb039813df273c44d053a08d124a9055b67cec00a1aeabd49c9a04b1c41e9fac len=1638
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note OM-2 qualification driver for the CURRENT consumer om/sha256/sha256.om (baseline acb3f15).
note The gate concatenates this file with om/sha256/sha256.om into one program-mode unit. It is
note test scaffolding, not a SHA implementation: every hash operation is the consumer's omsha.
note   stdin   the message, read to end of file
note   arg 1   optional piece size 1..4096 (default 4096): each read asks for at most that many bytes
note           and every byte read is absorbed with op 1, so the split points are exercised
note   stdout  the digest as 64 lowercase hex digits and a newline; exit 0
note Exit 90: bad argument; 91: read error; 92: short stdout write.
note digest byte j: the consumer packs the 32 digest bytes little endian into w[0..4)
fn dbyte w view ulong 64 j ulong to ulong
v = get w div j 8
ret and shr v mul rem j 8 8 255
end
text hexdig "0123456789abcdef"
fn piece to ulong
if eq argcnt 1
ret 4096
end
a = new uchar 8 0
r = argread 1 a 0 8
if or lt r 1 gt r 4
exit 90
end
v = ulong 0
for i ulong ulong r
d = get a i
if or lt d 48 gt d 57
exit 90
end
v = add mul v 10 ulong sub d 48
end
if or eq v 0 gt v 4096
exit 90
end
ret v
end
fn main to int
c = new uchar 104 0
b = new uchar 4096 0
w = new ulong 64 0
b8 = new ulong 512 0
o = new uchar 65 10
k = piece
omsha c b 0 0 w b8
go = true
while go
r = read 0 b 0 k
if lt r 0
ret 91
end
if eq r 0
go = false
else
omsha c b ulong r 1 w b8
end
end
omsha c b 0 2 w b8
for j ulong 32
x = dbyte w j
p = mul j 2
put o p get hexdig shr x 4
put o add p 1 get hexdig and x 15
end
r = write 1 o 0 65
if ne r 65
ret 92
end
ret 0
end

#### c2-05726 sha256=deb5b82bf1b9b36ec607c45e055ecf05b59fc2a889d4188493b47f7f4950f5ec len=25712
